From 0a10c9c5f7f7ffd4418ce9d444c52b022d58574c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: nhat092005 <minhnhat092005@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 9 Jun 2026 16:05:15 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] ARM: OMAP2+: skip voltage init on AM33xx and AM43xx

Upstream-Status: Pending [needs review for legacy mach-omap2 PM users]

AM33xx and AM43xx build the common OMAP voltage layer but do not provide
legacy voltage-domain data in mach-omap2. The common PM late init path
therefore calls omap_voltage_late_init() with an empty voltage-domain
list and emits a misleading boot error.

Skip the legacy voltage late init on these SoCs. Their PM setup continues
through the pm33xx platform path, while OMAP generations that provide
voltage-domain data keep the existing behavior.

Signed-off-by: nhat092005 <minhnhat092005@gmail.com>
---
 arch/arm/mach-omap2/pm.c | 7 ++++++-
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm/mach-omap2/pm.c b/arch/arm/mach-omap2/pm.c
index 700869c..5521f2f 100644
--- a/arch/arm/mach-omap2/pm.c
+++ b/arch/arm/mach-omap2/pm.c
@@ -145,7 +145,12 @@ static int __init omap2_common_pm_late_init(void)
 	omap3_twl_init();
 	omap4_twl_init();
 	omap4_cpcap_init();
-	omap_voltage_late_init();
+	/*
+	 * AM33xx and AM43xx do not provide legacy voltage-domain data in
+	 * mach-omap2. Their PM support is handled by the pm33xx platform path.
+	 */
+	if (!soc_is_am33xx() && !soc_is_am43xx())
+		omap_voltage_late_init();
 
 	/* Smartreflex device init */
 	omap_devinit_smartreflex();
-- 
